        "Tewahedo — Athanasius of Alexandria",
        "Athanasius of Alexandria (350).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Athanasius of Alexandria</strong> <em>Orationes contra Arianos I.46-47</em> <small>(c. 350 AD)</small><p>&#x27;How God anointed Jesus of Nazareth with the Holy Ghost and with power: who went about doing good, and healing all that were oppressed of the devil; for God was with him&#x27; — Athanasius marks echrisen auton ho theos Pneumati Hagiō (God-anointed him with-Spirit) as the COMMUNICATIO-IDIOMATUM Petrine-anchor. Christ qua-his-assumed-humanity is anointed-by-the-Spirit at the Jordan-baptism (Mt 3:17) and goes about healing-by-the-anointed-Spirit-in-him. Christ qua-his-divinity is the co-source of the Spirit with-the-Father. The same Person anoints and is-anointed; same-Person is Spirit-sender and Spirit-recipient.</p></aside>',
        "Athanasius of Alexandria, Orationes contra Arianos (Four Discourses Against the Arians, I-IV), in Select Writings and Letters of Athanasius, Nicene and Post-Nicene Fathers (NPNF), Series 2, Vol. 4, ed. Archibald Robertson (Oxford / T&T Clark, 1892). PD. Greek text in Migne PG 26 (1857).",
