        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>BAR-JESUS</strong> son of Joshua, the patronymic of Elymas the sorcerer (Acts 13:6), who met Paul and Barnabas at Paphos. Elymas is a word of Arabic origin meaning “wise.” <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
