        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>MACEDONIA</strong> in New Testament times, was a Roman province lying north of Greece. It was governed by a propraetor with the title of proconsul. Paul was summoned by the vision of the “man of Macedonia” to preach the gospel there (Acts 16:9). Frequent allusion is made to this event (18:5; 19:21; Romans 15:26; 2 Corinthians 1:16; 11:9; Phil. 4:15). The history of Paul’s first journey through Macedonia is given in detail in Acts 16:10-17:15. At the close of this journey he returned from… <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
