        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>NEAPOLIS</strong> new city, a town in Thrace at which Paul first landed in Europe (Acts 16:11). It was the sea-port of the inland town of Philippi, which was distant about 10 miles. From this port Paul embarked on his last journey to Jerusalem (Acts 20:6). It is identified with the modern Turco-Grecian Kavalla. <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
