        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>THESSALONIANS</strong> , EPISTLES TO THE The first epistle to the Thessalonians was the first of all Paul’s epistles. It was in all probability written from Corinth, where he abode a “long time” (Acts 18:11, 18), early in the period of his residence there, about the end of A.D. 52. The occasion of its being written was the return of Timotheus from Macedonia, bearing tidings from Thessalonica regarding the state of the church there (Acts 18:1-5; 1 Thessalonians 3:6). While, on the whole, the report… <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
